WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.310
- To me, art is like a gift, you know?

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:06.510
If you have capacity, if you have talent,

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:08.180
if you have grit and hard work

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:09.530
and you want to produce,

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:11.320
gifts are supposed to be given.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:12.460
So what's the point of giving a gift

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:15.230
if no one gets it, right?

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:17.370
What's the point of producing a symphony

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:19.320
if no one gets to hear it?

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:20.930
So I think reception is important

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:23.530
to give the art point,

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:26.010
meaning, as opposed to pointless.

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:26.843
You know?

00:00:26.843 --> 00:00:28.720
Otherwise, you're just
decorating your home.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.150
Now, we could have a debate whether

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:33.943
I'm receiving it myself, right?

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.007
So we could definitely debate that.

00:00:37.007 --> 00:00:37.840
But

00:00:39.232 --> 00:00:40.830
I think,

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:43.360
and maybe this is just the romantic in me,

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:44.940
it has to be enjoyed.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:47.450
And maybe one person is fine.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:48.900
Maybe if you hang it in your own home

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.690
and it's just for you, that's fine too.

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:52.670
But I think art has to be enjoyed,

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:53.820
otherwise what's the point?

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.653
You know?

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:58.820
Otherwise it's just therapy, you know?

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:00.550
I'm just painting for therapy.

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:02.600
And we all do things like that, you know?

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:07.090
Art has to have another
human being involved.

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:09.720
Or to me, art is about
a relationship, right?

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:12.780
You can't call yourself a romantic

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:15.360
or somebody who chooses to love another

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:17.323
if nobody ever feels your love.

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:20.280
You know?

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:23.390
It's, I think art is,

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:25.820
it's a type of language, right?

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:27.170
I know

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:28.003
people

00:01:28.003 --> 00:01:28.870
who

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:30.510
are the world's worst communicators

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:31.710
when it comes to their emotions

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:34.080
when you have a conversation with them.

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:35.280
I've dated some of them.

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:38.800
But given the opportunity to write,

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:40.663
it's magical.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.640
And the feelings pour out on the page

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:45.700
in an eloquence like I've never seen.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:47.330
And as everyone here knows,

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:49.470
great art in some way, shape, or form

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:52.760
is always personal or
semi-autobiographical.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:56.010
It's too hard to write
pure fiction, you know?

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:57.620
We put ourselves in it

00:01:57.620 --> 00:01:59.990
because it gives it a sense of reality

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:01.130
and it's what makes us passionate

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:03.760
for the subject that we're tackling.

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:05.420
I know dancers who, you know,

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:06.900
you meet them and they're like this

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:08.390
but as soon as they start dancing,

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:10.900
you realize it's all there.

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:12.660
So, art is language.

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:13.860
And if no one hears you,

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:16.070
you know if a tree falls in the woods,

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:19.020
you know, if no one
hears what you're saying,

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:20.260
is it worth saying anything?

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:22.110
They're just thoughts.

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:23.180
So what's the point of writing a play

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:24.013
that never gets shown?

00:02:24.013 --> 00:02:25.450
It's just a thought, you know?

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.290
It's just an intention.

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:28.919
So, yeah no, I think it must be shared.

00:02:28.919 --> 00:02:31.593
It's one of the ways in
which people communicate.

